Tuesday Update
* Trade Alert: Sold BLNK calls for solid gain; sell rest now. Buy DG and OX=
Y calls* Stocks swirl as coronavirus fears intensify and US economic data w=
orsensStocks are edging higher Tuesday as investors balanced prospects of e=
conomic improvement fueled by stimulus with concerns about a pandemic that =
continues to worsen.Through 2:30 pm ET, the Dow was up 70 points, or 0.2%, =
while the S&amp;P 500 was up 0.1%, the Nasdaq is up 0.3% and the Smallcap 6=
00 is up 1.5%.Small business sentiment index tracked by the National Federa=
tion of Independent Businesses declined 5.5 points in December to 95.9. Ian=
 Shepherdson, chief economist at Pantheon Macroeconomics, said firms cut th=
eir capital spending plans due to covid-19 fears, adding: =E2=80=9CThe serv=
ices economy cannot recover until the pandemic is over."While cases of the =
respiratory disease have been on the upswing in recent months, stimulus cou=
ld soon help the economy, according to analysts. "So far, real-time data do=
 not bode well for January, but we still believe that the inflection point =
is imminent, Jefferies economists Aneta Markowska and Thomas Simons wrote.C=
rude prices surged to levels seen before the pandemic slammed into the glob=
al economy. The sector was up 3% to lead the six of the 11 S&amp;P groups i=
nto the green.Portfolio: Sold new BLNK calls for a nice 33% gain; sell rest=
